{%- comment -%}
  Price contrast / inspired-by — 5 variants.

  Styles: ../component-library/css/components.css (.inspired, .ctable)

  Variants (the `contrast_style` argument):
    inline    .inspired             One line under the price. PDP default.
    callout   .inspired--callout    Small pill on a product card.
    table     .ctable               Two columns: Original | Siwa.
    story     .inspired--story      A paragraph making the case.
    footnote  .inspired--footnote   Small print at the foot of the PDP.

  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ⚠ TWO DELIBERATE DEFAULTS — DO NOT "FIX" THEM
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  1. `show_comparison` defaults FALSE. Nothing renders until a merchant
     switches it on.

  2. `show_retail_price` defaults FALSE, and is a SEPARATE setting from
     the module itself. With it off, the module renders "Inspired by
     <House> <Fragrance>" and no number.

  WHY. Making the dupe claim louder is a legal posture decision, not a
  design one. Oakcha operates in the US; Siwa operates in Egypt. The
  brief for this module is explicit: get legal counsel before shipping
  the retail price comparison. The module works without the number.
  Source: reference-analysis/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md §7.4.

  Additionally: the original-retail figures in the component library are
  ILLUSTRATIVE PLACEHOLDERS, not sourced (component-library/README.md).
  There is no verified retail price data in this repository. Turning
  `show_retail_price` on without sourcing real figures publishes numbers
  nobody has checked.

  ⚠ INSPIRED-BY PRODUCTS ONLY — ENFORCED IN CODE
  Rendering this on one of the 16 Originals would claim a Siwa original
  is a copy of something. The snippet resolves the register itself and
  renders NOTHING on an Original, whatever the caller asked for.

  ⚠ THE DATA DOES NOT EXIST YET
  `inspired_by.*` metafields are a recommendation; the store has zero
  custom metafields (03-DATA-SCHEMA.md §7). Today the house name falls
  back to `product.vendor`, which does hold the designer fragrance name.
  `retail_price` has no source at all and will be blank.

  Accepts:
    product           {Product}  required
    contrast_style    {String}   inline | callout | table | story | footnote
    show_comparison   {Boolean}  default FALSE — see above
    show_retail_price {Boolean}  default FALSE — see above
    disclaimer        {String}   trademark/comparison disclaimer text
    disclaimer_url    {String}   link to the full policy page
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  unless show_comparison
    break
  endunless

  capture register_raw
    render 'product-register', product: product
  endcapture
  assign register = register_raw | strip

  assign house = product.metafields.inspired_by.house | default: product.vendor
  assign fragrance = product.metafields.inspired_by.fragrance
  assign retail = product.metafields.inspired_by.retail_price

  assign cs = contrast_style | default: 'inline'
  case cs
    when 'callout'
      assign modifier = 'inspired--callout'
    when 'story'
      assign modifier = 'inspired--story'
    when 'footnote'
      assign modifier = 'inspired--footnote'
    else
      assign modifier = ''
  endcase

  assign show_retail = false
  if show_retail_price and retail != blank
    assign show_retail = true
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  The firewall: nothing renders on an Original, and nothing renders
  without a house to name.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if register == 'inspired' and house != blank -%}

  {%- if cs == 'table' -%}
    <table class="ctable">
      <caption class="visually-hidden">
        {{ 'products.contrast.table_caption' | t: product: product.title }}
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">&nbsp;</th>
          <th scope="col">{{ 'products.contrast.original' | t }}</th>
          <th scope="col">{{ shop.name }}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{{ 'products.contrast.fragrance' | t }}</th>
          <td>{{ house }}{% if fragrance != blank %} {{ fragrance }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ product.title }}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- if show_retail -%}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ 'products.contrast.price' | t }}</th>
            <td>{{ retail | money }}</td>
            <td>{{ product.price | money }}</td>
          </tr>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if product.selected_or_first_available_variant.title != blank -%}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ 'products.product.size' | t }}</th>
            <td>&mdash;</td>
            <td>{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.title }}</td>
          </tr>
        {%- endif -%}
      </tbody>
    </table>

  {%- elsif cs == 'story' -%}
    <div class="inspired {{ modifier }}">
      <p>
        {{ 'products.contrast.story' | t:
             house: house,
             fragrance: fragrance,
             product: product.title }}
      </p>
      {%- if show_retail -%}
        <p class="inspired__retail">
          {{ 'products.contrast.retail' | t }} {{ retail | money }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

  {%- else -%}
    <p class="inspired {{ modifier }}">
      <span class="inspired__label">{{ 'products.product.inspired_by' | t }}</span>
      <span class="inspired__house">
        {{ house }}{% if fragrance != blank %} {{ fragrance }}{% endif %}
      </span>
      {%- if show_retail -%}
        <span class="inspired__retail">
          &middot; {{ 'products.contrast.retail' | t }} {{ retail | money }}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if disclaimer != blank -%}
        <span class="inspired__note">
          {{ disclaimer }}
          {%- if disclaimer_url != blank -%}
            <a href="{{ disclaimer_url }}">{{ 'products.contrast.learn_more' | t }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}

{%- endif -%}
